; sum and total each name chez-adder in their tuna.deps, sum at commit 1
; and total at commit 3, which descends from it. Tuna installs commit 3
; and builds it before the configuration runs, and Chez finds (adder)
; through the library's own folders, with no wrapper.
> (sum:total 1 2)
3
> (total:version)
"3"
> (import (adder))
> (adder-sum 2 3)
5
; The build ran make in the library's folder with SCHEME set to Tuna's
; own Chez, which accepts -q before --script.
> adder-built-with
"Chez Scheme Version 10.4.1"
; Chez compiled the library into the library's own object folder.
> (file-exists? "~/.local/share/tuna/libraries/chez-adder/build/obj/src/adder.so")
#t
> (call-with-input-file "~/.local/share/tuna/libraries/chez-adder/.git/HEAD" get-line)
"98df19ef22eab6a1dea702a65ef28cc5224dac60"
; odd asks for commit 2, on another branch: no commit descends from all
; three, so the library is refused, naming the line to add, and the loaded
; library stays.
> (use-plugin odd (git "https://github.com/bob/odd"))
! use-plugin: plugin odd needs library chez-adder: plugin sum asks for chez-adder at commit 4c9b8c7, plugin total at commit 98df19e and plugin odd at commit 3fb7025, and none descends from all the others; add (library chez-adder (commit "...")) to init.ss
> (adder-version)
"3"
; A line typed at the REPL wins over every plugin's. The library is
; loaded, so the change waits for the next start.
> (library chez-adder (commit "3fb7025"))
! library: the REPL's line for library chez-adder replaces that of plugin sum
! library: the REPL's line for library chez-adder replaces that of plugin total
! library: library chez-adder is loaded, so its new line takes effect when Tuna starts again
> (adder-version)
"3"
; A library line is data, never Chez's library form.
> (library chez-adder (local))
! library: expected an id and clauses (git url) with (commit hex), (local folder), (library-directories root ...) or (build program argument ...) (library chez-adder (local))
